An absolute path is taken verbatim — no plugin-root join — and its render is written to stdout,
frontmatter and all, with the config values substituted.

`/proc/self/cwd` is how a case names a file it seeded: the sandbox path is generated per run, so it
cannot be spelled in a `cmd` line, and a relative path would resolve against the plugin root instead
of here. Every other case in this directory names its own template the same way.

-- fixtures/cwd/probe.md.j2 --
threshold {{ config.core.sprint.default_threshold_sp }}
redecompose {{ config.core.sprint.redecompose_threshold }}
-- cmd --
booping render /proc/self/cwd/probe.md.j2
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
threshold 35
redecompose 5
-- stderr --
